  "sympy_symbolic_integrals": {
    "s1_exact_token_weighted": "c0*((M*c0 + 1)*(M*c0 + (M*c0 + U)*log(M*c0 + U)) - (M*c0 + U)*(M*c0 + (M*c0 + 1)*log(M*c0 + 1)))/((M*c0 + 1)*(M*c0 + U))",
    "s1_piecewise_head": "c0/2 - 1/(2*M**2*c0)",
    "s1_piecewise_tail": "log((U/(M*c0))**c0)",
    "s1_piecewise_total": "c0/2 + log(U**(2*c0)/(M*c0)**(2*c0))/2 - 1/(2*M**2*c0)",
    "s1_key_averaged": "(-M**2*c0**2*(M*c0 + 1) + M**2*c0**2*(M*c0 + U) - (M*c0 + 1)*(M*c0 + U)*(-U + log((M*c0 + U)**(2*M*c0)/(M*c0 + 1)**(2*M*c0)) + 1))/(U*(M*c0 + 1)*(M*c0 + U))",
    "general_s_neq_1_tail": "Piecewise((c0*(-U**(1 - s) + (M*c0)**((1 - s)/s))/(s - 1), (s > 1) | (s < 1)), (log((U/(M*c0)**(1/s))**c0), True))",
    "interpretation": "For s=1 with fixed c0 (unnormalized truncated tail on [1, U]), token-weighted integral gives c0 * (ln((U + c0*M)/(1 + c0*M)) - ... ) ~ c0 * ln(U/(c0*M)) = c0*ln(U/M) - c0*ln(c0) when 1 << c0*M << U. If normalized on [1, U] so c0 = 1/ln(U), the leading term becomes 1 - ln(M/ln U)/ln U (not pure ln(U/M)). For general s != 1, the tail scales as power-law (c0/(1-s))*(U^(1-s) - (c0*M)^((1-s)/s)), not ln(U/M). Key-averaged MSE scales as 1 - O((c0*M/U)*ln(U/(c0*M))), not logarithmic."
  },
